## 5. Temporal Sequence Construction

```mermaid
flowchart TB
	A[Timestamped flow records] --> B{Group by Src IP}
	B --> C[Floor timestamps to window size<br/>default: 10 seconds]
	C --> D[Mean of 32 numeric features]
	D --> E[Max attack and tactic code per window]
	E --> F[Sort each source timeline]
	F --> G[Sliding window length T<br/>default: 15]
	G --> H[Input X: T historical states]
	G --> I[Target y: state at T+1]
	G --> J[Target y: attack at T+1]
	G --> K[Target y: tactic at T+1]
```

The model input is:

```text
X.shape = (number_of_sequences, T, 32)
```

For each sequence, the next window is supervised through three targets:

- `state`: the next 32 continuous feature values;
- `attack`: the next specific attack class code;
- `tactic`: the next high-level MITRE ATT&CK tactic code.

Short timelines are left-padded with zero-valued windows so that the model always receives the configured sequence length.

