## 7. Autoregressive Forecasting

```mermaid
flowchart TD
	A[Latest observed sequence] --> B[Model prediction]
	B --> C[Next state]
	B --> D[Tactic probability vector]
	D --> E[Weighted risk score]
	D --> F[Dominant tactic]
	C --> G[Remove oldest window]
	G --> H[Append predicted state]
	H --> I{More than K steps?}
	I -- Yes --> B
	I -- No --> J[Return forecast package]
	E --> J
	F --> J
```

At each step, the predicted continuous state replaces the oldest state in the input sequence. This makes the forecast forward-looking, but it also means errors can compound over long horizons. The dashboard should therefore emphasize near-term lead time and uncertainty rather than treating distant steps as certain outcomes.

The inference package contains:

```text
{
  "K": integer,
  "risk_timeline": [float, ...],
  "tactics": [string, ...],
  "top_features": {feature_name: score, ...}
}
```

