## 8. User Interface and Operational Workflow

```mermaid
flowchart LR
	A[Analyst] --> B[Upload PCAP / CSV]
	B --> C[Telemetry diagnostics]
	C --> D[Configure K, T, and window size]
	D --> E[Run forecast]
	E --> F[Current and peak risk]
	E --> G[Infiltration trajectory]
	E --> H[Top driving features]
	E --> I[MITRE progression]
	E --> J[Latest telemetry snapshot]
```

The dashboard has two runtime modes:

- **Checkpoint mode:** loads `models/saved/best_world_model.keras` and performs TensorFlow inference.
- **Simulation mode:** displays a deterministic preview curve when no checkpoint is available, allowing the interface to be demonstrated without a trained model.

Uploaded files are written to temporary storage for parsing and removed after ingestion. The resulting normalized dataframe and sequence cache remain in Streamlit session state to avoid repeating extraction when only forecast settings change.

