## 10. Training and Evaluation Architecture

```mermaid
flowchart LR
	A[Prepared CIC-style CSV<br/>or synthetic PCAP] --> B[Feature extraction]
	B --> C[Sequence and labels]
	C --> D[Train CNN-BiLSTM]
	D --> E[Saved Keras checkpoint]
	C --> F[Logistic regression baseline]
	E --> G[Inference evaluation]
	F --> H[Baseline metrics]
	G --> I[Compare temporal forecast<br/>with static classification]
	H --> I
```

The baseline is intentionally retained because it answers a useful question: whether temporal context provides value beyond classifying one feature vector. Evaluation should report, at minimum, attack classification performance, tactic classification performance, next-state error, and forecast lead time at selected risk thresholds.

